WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:06.180
This is Learn Text.js,
chapter five: Routing.

2
00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:12.090
In this chapter, you'll split Acme
Deploys into routes that share one layout.

3
00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:15.690
The App Router maps files
in the app folder to URLs,

4
00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:18.730
following the Next.js
App Router conventions.

5
00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:22.780
It matches the current path to a page,
and keeps the browser's address bar

6
00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:26.650
and history in sync, while
the UI stays in the console.

7
00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:30.380
Back, forward and deep links all work.

8
00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:34.380
Let's start with files.

9
00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:42.250
Folders in app are route segments, and a
page.tsx file makes a segment routable.

10
00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:46.010
The page.tsx at the top renders at /.

11
00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:51.370
Move the list into a deployments folder,
and its page renders at /deployments.

12
00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:54.970
A folder name in square
brackets is a dynamic segment.

13
00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:59.770
This one matches any
deployment ID, like dpl_8fK2.

14
00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:03.500
And a settings page renders at /settings.

15
00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:09.060
Next, a layout every page shares.

16
00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:15.230
layout.tsx wraps every page, and it stays
mounted while you move between them.

17
00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:17.870
Put the top bar and the navigation in it.

18
00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:22.350
metadata sets the document
title: Acme Deploys by default,

19
00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.990
and a template for pages
that set their own.

20
00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:30.590
usePathname returns the current path, and
the top bar shows it after acme.local.

21
00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:35.150
Link comes from @textjs/app/link.

22
00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:39.870
shortcut binds a single key to
each link: one, two and three.

23
00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:43.550
The current page renders as
children, below the navigation.

24
00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:47.760
Save, and every route
renders inside this layout.

25
00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:54.950
useRouter navigates from code, with
push, replace, back and forward.

26
00:01:55.000 --> 00:02:01.830
Import useInput from @textjs/app,
and useRouter next to usePathname.

27
00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:07.400
Get the router in the layout, and when
the key is backspace, call router.back().

28
00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:11.110
Here it is, on the lesson page.

29
00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:14.230
Click the pad first,
so the page has focus.

30
00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:17.670
Press two for deployments,
and three for settings.

31
00:02:17.720 --> 00:02:19.910
The top bar follows the path.

32
00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:24.520
Backspace goes back to deployments,
and back again to the overview.

33
00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:29.960
Last, dynamic segments.

34
00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:34.710
A dynamic segment receives
its value in params.

35
00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:41.030
Import the PageProps type from @textjs/app,
and give it the shape of your params.

36
00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:43.270
Render the ID in bold.

37
00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:52.630
At /deployments/dpl_8fK2, params.id
is dpl_8fK2, inside the same layout.

38
00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:54.790
Deep links work with text dev.

39
00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:58.590
A static host needs a rewrite for
dynamic segments like this one,

40
00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:01.080
and chapter ten covers it.

41
00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:03.870
Quick check.

42
00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:07.600
Which file renders at /deployments?

43
00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:13.350
app/deployments/page.tsx.

44
00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:18.230
Folders are segments, and
page.tsx makes a segment routable,

45
00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:21.640
as in the Next.js App Router.

46
00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:26.680
And what survives
navigation between pages?

47
00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:29.450
Layout state.

48
00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:33.340
Layouts stay mounted
while their pages change.

49
00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:39.370
Next, in chapter six, you'll serve
deployments from a route handler,

50
00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:42.010
fetch them in a page, and post new ones.

51
00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:43.740
See you there.
